(window.IND_GITA_V = window.IND_GITA_V || {})[14] = [{"v":1,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":"श्री भगवानुवाच","spp":"before","sa":"परं भूयः प्रवक्ष्यामि ज्ञानानां ज्ञानमुत्तमम् ।\nयज्ज्ञात्वा मुनयः सर्वे परां सिद्धिमितो गताः ॥","iast":"paraṃ bhūyaḥ pravakṣyāmi jñānānāṃ jñānamuttamam |\nyajjñātvā munayaḥ sarve parāṃ siddhimito gatāḥ ||","read":"param bhooyah pravakshyaami jnaanaanaam jnaanamuttamam |\nyajjnaatvaa munayah sarve paraam siddhimito gataah ||","spli":"śrī bhagavānuvāca","splr":"shree bhagavaanuvaacha","en":"The Blessed Lord said: I will again proclaim that supreme Wisdom, of all wisdom the best, which having known, all the Sages have gone hence to the supreme Perfection.","en2":"Again shall I tell thee that supreme knowledge which is above all knowledge, having known which all the Munis have attained to high perfection after this life.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":2,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"इदं ज्ञानमुपाश्रित्य मम साधर्म्यमागताः ।\nसर्गेऽपि नोपजायन्ते प्रलये न व्यथन्ति च ॥","iast":"idaṃ jñānamupāśritya mama sādharmyamāgatāḥ |\nsarge’pi nopajāyante pralaye na vyathanti ca ||","read":"idam jnaanamupaashritya mama saadharmyamaagataah |\nsarge'pi nopajaayante pralaye na vyathanti cha ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Having taken refuge in this Wisdom and being assimilated to My own nature, they are not re-born even in the emanation of a universe, nor are disquieted in the dissolution.","en2":"They who having devoted themselves to this knowledge, have attained to My Being, are neither born at the time of creation, nor are they troubled at the time of dissolution.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":3,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"मम योनिर्महद्ब्रह्म तस्मिन् गर्भं दधाम्यहम् ।\nसंभवः सर्वभूतानां ततो भवति भारत ॥","iast":"mama yonirmahadbrahma tasmin garbhaṃ dadhāmyaham |\nsaṃbhavaḥ sarvabhūtānāṃ tato bhavati bhārata ||","read":"mama yonirmahadbrahma tasmin garbham dadhaamyaham |\nsambhavah sarvabhootaanaam tato bhavati bhaarata ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"My womb is the great Eternal; in that I place the germ; thence cometh the birth of all beings, O Bhârata.","en2":"My womb is the great Prakriti; in that I place the germ; from thence, O descendant of Bharata, is the birth of all beings.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":4,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"सर्वयोनिषु कौन्तेय मूर्तयः सम्भवन्ति याः ।\nतासां ब्रह्म महद्योनिरहं बीजप्रदः पिता ॥","iast":"sarvayoniṣu kaunteya mūrtayaḥ sambhavanti yāḥ |\ntāsāṃ brahma mahadyonirahaṃ bījapradaḥ pitā ||","read":"sarvayonishu kaunteya moortayah sambhavanti yaah |\ntaasaam brahma mahadyoniraham beejapradah pitaa ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"In whatsoever wombs mortals are produced, O Kaunteya, the great Eternal is their womb, I their generating father.","en2":"Whatever forms are produced, O son of Kunti, in all the wombs, the great Prakriti is their womb, and I the seed-giving Father.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":5,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"सत्त्वं रजस्तम इति गुणाः प्रकृतिसंभवाः ।\nनिबध्नन्ति महाबाहो देहे देहिनमव्ययम् ॥","iast":"sattvaṃ rajastama iti guṇāḥ prakṛtisaṃbhavāḥ |\nnibadhnanti mahābāho dehe dehinamavyayam ||","read":"sattvam rajastama iti gunaah prakritisambhavaah |\nnibadhnanti mahaabaaho dehe dehinamavyayam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Harmony, Motion, Inertia, such are the qualities, Matter-born; they bind fast in the body, O great-armed one, the indestructible dweller in the body.","en2":"Sattva, Rajas, and Tamas,—these Gunas, O mighty-armed, born of Prakriti, bind fast in the body the indestructible embodied one.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":6,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"तत्र सत्त्वं निर्मलत्वात्प्रकाशकमनामयम् ।\nसुखसङ्गेन बध्नाति ज्ञानसङ्गेन चानघ ॥","iast":"tatra sattvaṃ nirmalatvātprakāśakamanāmayam |\nsukhasaṅgena badhnāti jñānasaṅgena cānagha ||","read":"tatra sattvam nirmalatvaatprakaashakamanaamayam |\nsukhasangena badhnaati jnaanasangena chaanagha ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Of these Harmony from its stainlessness, luminous and healthy, bindeth by the attachment to bliss and the attachment to wisdom, O sinless one.","en2":"Of these Sattva, from its stainlessness luminous and free from evil, binds, O sinless one, by attachment to happiness, and by attachment to knowledge.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":7,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"रजो रागात्मकं विद्धि तृष्णासङ्गसमुद्भवम् ।\nतन्निबध्नाति कौन्तेय कर्मसङ्गेन देहिनम् ॥","iast":"rajo rāgātmakaṃ viddhi tṛṣṇāsaṅgasamudbhavam |\ntannibadhnāti kaunteya karmasaṅgena dehinam ||","read":"rajo raagaatmakam viddhi trishnaasangasamudbhavam |\ntannibadhnaati kaunteya karmasangena dehinam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Motion, the passion nature, know thou, is the source of attachment and thirst for life, O Kaunteya, that bindeth the dweller in the body by the attachment to action.","en2":"Know Rajas to be of the nature of passion, giving rise to thirst and attachment; it binds fast, O son of Kunti, the embodied one, by attachment to action.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":8,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"तमस्त्वज्ञानजं विद्धि मोहनं सर्वदेहिनाम् ।\nप्रमादालस्यनिद्राभिस्तन्निबध्नाति भारत ॥","iast":"tamastvajñānajaṃ viddhi mohanaṃ sarvadehinām |\npramādālasyanidrābhistannibadhnāti bhārata ||","read":"tamastvajnaanajam viddhi mohanam sarvadehinaam |\npramaadaalasyanidraabhistannibadhnaati bhaarata ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"But Inertia, know thou, born of unwisdom, is the deluder of all dwellers in the body; that bindeth by heedlessness, indolence and sloth, O Bharata.","en2":"And know Tamas to be born of ignorance, stupefying all embodied beings; it binds fast, O descendant of Bharata, by miscomprehension, indolence, and sleep.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":9,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"सत्त्वं सुखे सञ्जयति रजः कर्मणि भारत ।\nज्ञानमावृत्य तु तमः प्रमादे सञ्जयत्युत ॥","iast":"sattvaṃ sukhe sañjayati rajaḥ karmaṇi bhārata |\njñānamāvṛtya tu tamaḥ pramāde sañjayatyuta ||","read":"sattvam sukhe sanjayati rajah karmani bhaarata |\njnaanamaavritya tu tamah pramaade sanjayatyuta ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Harmony attacheth to bliss, Motion to action O Bharata. Inertia, verily, having shrouded wisdom, attacheth on the contrary to heedlessness.","en2":"Sattva attaches to happiness, and Rajas to action, O descendant of Bharata; while Tamas, verily, shrouding discrimination, attaches to miscomprehension.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":10,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"रजस्तमश्चाभिभूय सत्त्वं भवति भारत ।\nरजः सत्त्वं तमश्चैव तमः सत्त्वं रजस्तथा ॥","iast":"rajastamaścābhibhūya sattvaṃ bhavati bhārata |\nrajaḥ sattvaṃ tamaścaiva tamaḥ sattvaṃ rajastathā ||","read":"rajastamashchaabhibhooya sattvam bhavati bhaarata |\nrajah sattvam tamashchaiva tamah sattvam rajastathaa ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Now Harmony prevaileth, having overpowered Motion and Inertia, O Bhârata; now Motion, having overpowered Harmony and Inertia; and now Inertia, having overpowered Harmony and Motion.","en2":"Sattva arises, O descendant of Bharata, predominating over Rajas and 'Tamas; and Rajas over Sattva and Tamas; so, Tamas over Sattva and Rajas.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":11,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"सर्वद्वारेषु देहेऽस्मिन्प्रकाश उपजायते ।\nज्ञानं यदा तदा विद्याद्विवृद्धं सत्त्वमित्युत ॥","iast":"sarvadvāreṣu dehe’sminprakāśa upajāyate |\njñānaṃ yadā tadā vidyādvivṛddhaṃ sattvamityuta ||","read":"sarvadvaareshu dehe'sminprakaasha upajaayate |\njnaanam yadaa tadaa vidyaadvivriddham sattvamityuta ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"When the wisdom-light streameth forth from all the gates of the body, then it may be known that Harmony is increasing.","en2":"When through every sense in this body, the light of intelligence shines, then it should be known that Sattva is predominant.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":12,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"लोभः प्रवृत्तिरारम्भः कर्मणामशमः स्पृहा ।\nरजस्येतानि जायन्ते विवृद्धे भरतर्षभ ॥","iast":"lobhaḥ pravṛttirārambhaḥ karmaṇāmaśamaḥ spṛhā |\nrajasyetāni jāyante vivṛddhe bharatarṣabha ||","read":"lobhah pravrittiraarambhah karmanaamashamah sprihaa |\nrajasyetaani jaayante vivriddhe bharatarshabha ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Greed, outgoing energy, undertaking of actions, restlessness, desire—these are born of the increase of Motion, O best of the Bhâratas.","en2":"Greed, activity, the undertaking of actions, unrest, longing—these arise when Rajas is predominant, O bull of the: Bhâratas.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":13,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अप्रकाशोऽप्रवृत्तिश्च प्रमादो मोह एव च ।\nतमस्येतानि जायन्ते विवृद्धे कुरुनन्दन ॥","iast":"aprakāśo’pravṛttiśca pramādo moha eva ca |\ntamasyetāni jāyante vivṛddhe kurunandana ||","read":"aprakaasho'pravrittishcha pramaado moha eva cha |\ntamasyetaani jaayante vivriddhe kurunandana ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Darkness, stagnation and heedlessness and also delusion—these are born of the increase of Inertia, O joy of the Kurus.","en2":"Darkness, inertness, miscomprehension, and delusion,—these arise when Tamas is predominant, O descendant of Kuru.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":14,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यदा सत्त्वे प्रवृद्धे तु प्रलयं याति देहभृत् ।\nतदोत्तमविदां लोकानमलान्प्रतिपद्यते ॥","iast":"yadā sattve pravṛddhe tu pralayaṃ yāti dehabhṛt |\ntadottamavidāṃ lokānamalānpratipadyate ||","read":"yadaa sattve pravriddhe tu pralayam yaati dehabhrit |\ntadottamavidaam lokaanamalaanpratipadyate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"If Harmony verily prevaileth when the embodied goeth to dissolution, then he goeth forth to the spotless worlds of the great Sages.","en2":"If the embodied one meets death when Sattva is predominant, then he attains to the spotless regions of the worshippers of the Highest.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":15,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"रजसि प्रलयं गत्वा कर्मसङ्गिषु जायते ।\nतथा प्रलीनस्तमसि मूढयोनिषु जायते ॥","iast":"rajasi pralayaṃ gatvā karmasaṅgiṣu jāyate |\ntathā pralīnastamasi mūḍhayoniṣu jāyate ||","read":"rajasi pralayam gatvaa karmasangishu jaayate |\ntathaa praleenastamasi moodhayonishu jaayate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Having gone to dissolution in Motion, he is born among those attached to action; if dissolved in Inertia, he is born in the wombs of the senseless.","en2":"Meeting death in Rajas he is born among those attached to action; so dying in Tamas, he is born in the wombs of the irrational.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":16,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"कर्मणः सुकृतस्याहुः सात्त्विकं निर्मलं फलम् ।\nरजसस्तु फलं दुःखमज्ञानं तमसः फलम् ॥","iast":"karmaṇaḥ sukṛtasyāhuḥ sāttvikaṃ nirmalaṃ phalam |\nrajasastu phalaṃ duḥkhamajñānaṃ tamasaḥ phalam ||","read":"karmanah sukritasyaahuh saattvikam nirmalam phalam |\nrajasastu phalam duhkhamajnaanam tamasah phalam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"It is said the fruit of a good action is harmonious and spotless; verily the fruit of Motion is pain, and the fruit of Inertia unwisdom","en2":"The fruit of good action, they say, is Sâttvika and pure; verily, the fruit of Rajas is pain, and ignorance is the fruit of Tamas.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":17,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"सत्त्वात्सञ्जायते ज्ञानं रजसो लोभ एव च ।\nप्रमादमोहौ तमसो भवतोऽज्ञानमेव च ॥","iast":"sattvātsañjāyate jñānaṃ rajaso lobha eva ca |\npramādamohau tamaso bhavato’jñānameva ca ||","read":"sattvaatsanjaayate jnaanam rajaso lobha eva cha |\npramaadamohau tamaso bhavato'jnaanameva cha ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"From Harmony wisdom is born, and also greed from Motion; heedlessness and delusion are of Inertia and also unwisdom.","en2":"From Sattva arises wisdom, and greed from Rajas; miscomprehension, delusion and ignorance arise from Tamas.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":18,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"ऊर्ध्वं गच्छन्ति सत्त्वस्था मध्ये तिष्ठन्ति राजसाः ।\nजघन्यगुणवृत्तिस्था अधो गच्छन्ति तामसाः ॥","iast":"ūrdhvaṃ gacchanti sattvasthā madhye tiṣṭhanti rājasāḥ |\njaghanyaguṇavṛttisthā adho gacchanti tāmasāḥ ||","read":"oordhvam gachchhanti sattvasthaa madhye tishthanti raajasaah |\njaghanyagunavrittisthaa adho gachchhanti taamasaah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"They rise upwards who are settled in Harmony; the Active dwell in the mid-most place: the Inert go downwards, enveloped in the vilest","en2":"The Sattva-abiding go upwards; the Râjasika dwell in the middle; and the Tâmasika, abiding in the function. of the lowest Guna, go downwards.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":19,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"नान्यं गुणेभ्यः कर्तारं यदा द्रष्टानुपश्यति ।\nगुणेभ्यश्च परं वेत्ति मद्भावं सोऽधिगच्छति ॥","iast":"nānyaṃ guṇebhyaḥ kartāraṃ yadā draṣṭānupaśyati |\nguṇebhyaśca paraṃ vetti madbhāvaṃ so’dhigacchati ||","read":"naanyam gunebhyah kartaaram yadaa drashtaanupashyati |\ngunebhyashcha param vetti madbhaavam so'dhigachchhati ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"When the Seer perceiveth no agent other than the qualities, and knoweth That which is higher than the qualities, he entereth into My Nature.","en2":"When the seer beholds no agent other than the Gunas and knows That which is higher than the Gunas, he attains to My being.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":20,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"गुणानेतानतीत्य त्रीन्देही देहसमुद्भवान् ।\nजन्ममृत्युजरादुःखैर्विमुक्तोऽमृतमश्नुते ॥","iast":"guṇānetānatītya trīndehī dehasamudbhavān |\njanmamṛtyujarāduḥkhairvimukto’mṛtamaśnute ||","read":"gunaanetaanateetya treendehee dehasamudbhavaan |\njanmamrityujaraaduhkhairvimukto'mritamashnute ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"When the dweller in the body hath crossed over these three qualities, whence all bodies have been produced, liberated from birth, death, old age and sorrow, he drinketh the nectar of immortality.","en2":"The embodied one having gone beyond these three Gunas out of which the body is evolved, is freed from birth, death, decay and pain, and attains to immortality.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":21,"sp":"arjuna","spm":null,"spl":"अर्जुन उवाच","spp":"before","sa":"कैर्लिंगैस्त्रीन्गुणानेतानतीतो भवति प्रभो ।\nकिमाचारः कथं चैतांस्त्रीन्गुणानतिवर्तते ॥","iast":"kairliṃgaistrīnguṇānetānatīto bhavati prabho |\nkimācāraḥ kathaṃ caitāṃstrīnguṇānativartate ||","read":"kairlimgaistreengunaanetaanateeto bhavati prabho |\nkimaachaarah katham chaitaamstreengunaanativartate ||","spli":"arjuna uvāca","splr":"arjuna uvaacha","en":"Arjuna said: What are the marks of him who hath crossed over the three qualities, O Lord? How acteth he, and how doth he go beyond these three qualities?","en2":"By what marks, O Lord, is he (known) who has gone beyond these three Gunas? What is his conduct, and how does he pass beyond these three Gunas?","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":22,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":"श्री भगवानुवाच","spp":"before","sa":"प्रकाशं च प्रवृत्तिं च मोहमेव च पाण्डव ।\nन द्वेष्टि सम्प्रवृत्तानि न निवृत्तानि काङ्क्षति ॥","iast":"prakāśaṃ ca pravṛttiṃ ca mohameva ca pāṇḍava |\nna dveṣṭi sampravṛttāni na nivṛttāni kāṅkṣati ||","read":"prakaasham cha pravrittim cha mohameva cha paandava |\nna dveshti sampravrittaani na nivrittaani kaankshati ||","spli":"śrī bhagavānuvāca","splr":"shree bhagavaanuvaacha","en":"The Blessed Lord said: He, O Pândava, who hateth not radiance, nor outgoing energy, nor even delusion, when present, nor longeth after them, absent;","en2":"He who hates not the appearance of light, (the effect of Sattva), activity (the effect of Rajas), and delusion (the effect of Tamas), (in his own mind), O Pândava, nor longs for them when absent;","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":23,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"उदासीनवदासीनो गुणैर्यो न विचाल्यते ।\nगुणा वर्तन्त इत्येव योऽवतिष्ठति नेङ्गते ॥","iast":"udāsīnavadāsīno guṇairyo na vicālyate |\nguṇā vartanta ityeva yo’vatiṣṭhati neṅgate ||","read":"udaaseenavadaaseeno gunairyo na vichaalyate |\ngunaa vartanta ityeva yo'vatishthati nengate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"He who, seated as a neutral, is unshaken by the qualities; who, saying, \"The qualities revolve,\" standeth apart immovable.","en2":"He who, sitting like one unconcerned, is moved not by the Gunas, who, knowing that the Gunas operate, is Self-centred and swerves not;","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":24,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"समदुःखसुखः स्वस्थः समलोष्टाश्मकाञ्चनः ।\nतुल्यप्रियाप्रियो धीरस्तुल्यनिन्दात्मसंस्तुतिः ॥","iast":"samaduḥkhasukhaḥ svasthaḥ samaloṣṭāśmakāñcanaḥ |\ntulyapriyāpriyo dhīrastulyanindātmasaṃstutiḥ ||","read":"samaduhkhasukhah svasthah samaloshtaashmakaanchanah |\ntulyapriyaapriyo dheerastulyanindaatmasamstutih ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Balanced in pleasure and pain, self-reliant, to whom a lump of earth, a rock and gold are alike, the same to loved and unloved, firm, the same in censure and in praise,","en2":"Alike in pleasure and pain, Self-abiding, regarding a clod of earth, a stone and gold alike; the same to agreeable and disagreeable, firm, the same in censure and, praise;","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":25,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"मानापमानयोस्तुल्यस्तुल्यो मित्रारिपक्षयोः ।\nसर्वारम्भपरित्यागी गुणातीतः स उच्यते ॥","iast":"mānāpamānayostulyastulyo mitrāripakṣayoḥ |\nsarvārambhaparityāgī guṇātītaḥ sa ucyate ||","read":"maanaapamaanayostulyastulyo mitraaripakshayoh |\nsarvaarambhaparityaagee gunaateetah sa uchyate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The same in honour and ignominy, the same to friend and foe, abandoning all undertakings—he is said to have crossed over the qualities.","en2":"The same in honour and disgrace, the same to friend and foe, relinquishing all undertakings—he is said to have gone beyond the Gunas.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":26,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"मां च योऽव्यभिचारेण भक्तियोगेन सेवते ।\nस गुणान्समतीत्यैतान् ब्रह्मभूयाय कल्पते ॥","iast":"māṃ ca yo’vyabhicāreṇa bhaktiyogena sevate |\nsa guṇānsamatītyaitān brahmabhūyāya kalpate ||","read":"maam cha yo'vyabhichaarena bhaktiyogena sevate |\nsa gunaansamateetyaitaan brahmabhooyaaya kalpate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"And he who serveth Me exclusively by the Yoga of devotion, he, crossing beyond the qualities, he is fit to become the Eternal.","en2":"And he who serves Me with an unswerving devotion, he, going beyond the Gunas, is fitted for becoming Brahman.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":27,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"ब्रह्मणो हि प्रतिष्ठाऽहममृतस्याव्ययस्य च ।\nशाश्वतस्य च धर्मस्य सुखस्यैकान्तिकस्य च ॥","iast":"brahmaṇo hi pratiṣṭhā’hamamṛtasyāvyayasya ca |\nśāśvatasya ca dharmasya sukhasyaikāntikasya ca ||","read":"brahmano hi pratishthaa'hamamritasyaavyayasya cha |\nshaashvatasya cha dharmasya sukhasyaikaantikasya cha ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"For I am the abode of the Eternal, and of the indestructible nectar of immortality, of immemorial righteousness, and of unending bliss.","en2":"For I am the abode of Brahman, the Immortal and Immutable, of everlasting Dharma and of Absolute Bliss.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null}];
